@startuml 22_state_audio_playback
!theme plain
!pragma layout smetana
title CAR-PC Audio Playback — Interruption, Queueing, and Feedback

state "Idle" as idle
state "Playing audio number n" as playing
state "Completed" as completed
state "Playback error" as error

[*] --> idle : AudioManager starts
idle : entry / publish position=-1, active=0 (CAN frame twice)
idle --> playing : Changed valid request n / play A[n] from 0
playing : entry / publish position=0, active=n
playing : Every T ms / publish elapsed_ms and active=n together
playing : Type 1 request m / stop n, clear queue, start m; publish 0 and m
playing : Type 2 request m / queue m; keep playing n and keep its position
playing : Track ends, queue not empty / pop FIFO, start next; publish 0 and next number
playing --> completed : Track ends successfully and queue empty
completed : entry / publish position=-1, active=0 (CAN frame twice)
completed --> playing : Changed valid request n / play A[n] from 0

idle --> error : File resolution or player startup fails
playing --> error : File/player failure
completed --> error : File resolution or player startup fails
error : entry / clear queue, publish position=-1, active=0 (CAN frame twice)
error --> playing : New valid request / start succeeds

legend bottom
  A = audio.files, addressed by audio_number (1..255).
  T = audio.position_update_interval_ms (50..60000).
  Type 1: audio.track_queue_enable=false. Type 2: true (FIFO max 64).

  Only changed, configured non-zero requests start or queue playback.
  0 re-arms the request; no stop and no queue clear. Disabled audio ignores requests.
  Replay the same number with an observed 0 -> number transition.

  Feedback frame: INC_HMI_Audio_Response (0x221)
  position = HMI_AudioTimesamp (elapsed ms, or -1 when inactive)
  active = HMI_ActiveSoundfile (audio_number, or 0 when inactive)
  HMI_Soundfile updates immediately; HMI_ActiveSoundfile follows actual playback.
  Queued tracks start directly without an idle -1 frame.
  A changed T takes effect on the next playback.
endlegend
@enduml
